# GIT & PR SAFETY RULES

- Always create a new feature/fix branch from main before making changes.
- Never commit or push directly to main.
- Never force-push.
- Never delete or rename existing branches unless the user explicitly asks.
- Prefer small, focused commits with clear messages.
- When asked to “handle the PR”, create the branch → make changes → commit → push → open a PR against main, then give the user the PR link.
- If the working tree is dirty or the user is on a messy branch, warn them and offer to start clean from main.
